      "description": "Crawl a site breadth-first, running the full auto_scrape cascade on each page \u2014 so every page benefits from recipe replay, the render tier, and proxy rotation, and the recipe learned on page one makes the rest cheap. robots.txt is honoured by default, including Crawl-delay. Bounded by depth / max_pages / concurrency, and the response reports what the bounds left unvisited. Page HTML is omitted by default: a 50-page crawl of rendered pages is tens of MB and would swamp the agent's context.",
